   "id": "P013",
   "texts": [
    "Create an Amazon EBS volume",
    "• A volume exists in an Availability Zone.",
    "• AWS Command Line Interface (AWS CLI) example:",
    "• Use the create-volume command",
    "• Use the –-availability-zone option to specify the Availability Zone",
    "$ aws ec2 create-volume –-size 80 \\",
    "–-availability-zone us-east-1a --volume-type gp2"
   ],
   "notes": [],
   "hidden": false,
   "rendered": [],
   "img": "img/p-13.jpg"
  },
  {
   "id": "P014",
   "texts": [
    "Describe new volume just created",
    "CLI command for describing the volume created:",
    "$ aws ec2 describe-volumes --volume-ids vol-0e5e5193f8d093d5f"
   ],
   "notes": [],
   "hidden": false,
   "rendered": [],
   "img": "img/p-14.jpg"
  },
  {
   "id": "P015",
   "texts": [
    "Attach an Amazon EBS volume",
    "• Attach volumes to logical mount points in the operating system",
    "• AWS CLI example:",
    "• Use the attach-volume command.",
    "• Use the –- device option to specify the mount point.",
    "$ aws ec2 attach-volume –-volume-id vol-12345678 \\",
    "--instance-id i-abc1234 –-device /dev/sdf"
   ],
   "notes": [],
   "hidden": false,
   "rendered": [],
   "img": "img/p-15.jpg"
  },
  {
   "id": "P016",
   "texts": [
    "Amazon EBS-optimized instances",
    "• Certain EC2 instance types can be EBS-optimized.",
    "• Provides a dedicated network connection to EBS",
    "volume",
    "• Increases performance of Amazon EBS I/O",
    "• For EBS-optimized instance types, optimization is",
    "enabled by default.",
    "• For other instances types that support it,",
    "optimization must be manually enabled.",
    "• Additional performance is achieved if using an",
    "Amazon EC2 Nitro System based instance type.",
