  {
   "id": "P018",
   "texts": [
    "Create a snapshot of an EBS volume",
    "• Use the AWS CLI command create-snapshot. The command returns",
    "asynchronously.",
    "• Consider stopping the instance or unmounting the volume first:",
    "• For completeness (otherwise, no subsequent writes are captured.)",
    "• Strongly recommended for volumes that serve as a root device",
    "• Critical for database servers and Redundant Array of Independent Disks (RAID)",
    "configurations",
    "aws ec2 create-snapshot –-volume-id vol-1234567890abcdef0",
    "--description \"This is my root volume snapshot\""
   ],
   "notes": [],
   "hidden": false,
   "rendered": [],
   "img": "img/p-18.jpg"
  },
  {
   "id": "P019",
   "texts": [
    "Copy a snapshot and proof of copy",
    "• Use the AWS CLI command",
    "copy-snapshot.",
    "• Data in transit is automatically",
    "encrypted.",
    "• New snapshot has a different ID",
    "from the original.",
    "CLI command: Copy a snapshot",
    "$ aws ec2 copy-snapshot –-region us-east-1 \\",
    "--source-region us-west-2 \\",
    "–-source-snapshot-id snap-1234567890abcdef0 \\",
    "--description \"This is my copied snapshot\"",
    "CLI command: Proof of copy to a new Region",
    "$ aws ec2 describe-snapshots \\",
    "--snapshot-ids snap-0b3c2a7c2a7e4eec6 \\",
    "--region us-east-1"
   ],
   "notes": [],
   "hidden": false,
   "rendered": [],
   "img": "img/p-19.jpg"
  },
  {
   "id": "P020",
   "texts": [
    "Restore a snapshot",
    "• Snapshot is stored in Amazon S3 but is",
    "not directly accessible. Managed by AWS.",
    "• Find the snapshot ID and restore to a new",
    "volume using the create-volume",
    "command.",
    "• Volumes restored from snapshots have a",
    "first-access penalty. Consider reading all",
    "the blocks to eliminate penalty in",
    "production.",
    "CLI command: Copy a snapshot",
    "$ aws ec2 create-volume \\",
    "–-size 80 \\",
    "–-availability-zone us-east-1a \\",
    "--volume-type gp2 \\",
    "–-snapshot-id snap-1234567890abcdef0"
   ],
   "notes": [],
   "hidden": false,
   "rendered": [],
   "img": "img/p-20.jpg"
  },
  {
   "id": "P021",
   "texts": [
    "Restore a snapshot",
    "• Snapshot is stored in Amazon S3 but is not",
    "directly accessible. Managed by AWS.",
    "• Find the snapshot ID, and restore it to a new",
    "volume using the",
    "create-volume command.",
    "• Volumes restored from snapshots have a firstaccess penalty. Consider reading all the blocks",
    "to eliminate the penalty in production.",
    "CLI command: Proof of copy to",
    "a new Region",
    "$ aws ec2 \\",
    "describe-volume-status \\",
    "--volume-ids vol-0c108c43c627cb26d"
   ],
